@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+# draft-person-date-of-birth: Add a date of birth to the person
+
+- **Jira:** none yet (direct request)
+- **Gate:** normal
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:** <GitHub login> <YYYY-MM-DD>
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: none
+
+## Context
+
+The person record has no date of birth. A direct request adds an optional date of birth to registration and to the person read.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+No Discovery AC covers this request, so the tests carry no AC ID yet. The request's criteria; 1, 3 and 4 are covered in `packages/core/src/identity/identity.test.ts` (`describe("date of birth")`), 2 by `schema.ts` and `pnpm pii`:
+
+1. `registerPerson` accepts an optional `dateOfBirth` (ISO date `YYYY-MM-DD`); a malformed value is rejected.
+2. The person table has a column `date_of_birth`, with personal data metadata.
+3. `getPerson` returns `dateOfBirth`, or `null` when it was not given.
+4. A date of birth in the future is rejected with an error (`Europe/Berlin` business date).
+
+When the Jira story has AC IDs, put them in this table and at the start of each test title.
+
+| ID | Test |
+|---|---|
+| none | `packages/core/src/identity/identity.test.ts` |
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** `.registerPerson({ email, givenName, familyName, dateOfBirth?, brand? })`; `.getPerson(id)` returns `dateOfBirth: string | null`; new export `InvalidDateOfBirthError`; new invariant on the date of birth.
+- **Contracts:** none. The `identity.person-registered` payload does not change.
+- **Schema:** `identity.person.date_of_birth`, `date` (string mode), nullable. Personal: yes, category `identity` (existing), purpose "Identify the person", owner `identity`, retention `account lifetime + 3 years`.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- Gate normal: the new column is personal but uses the existing category `identity` (AGENTS.md design trigger 3).
+- "Future" means after today's `Europe/Berlin` business date (`kernel.businessDate`), per the data conventions; today itself is accepted.
+- A malformed value (not `YYYY-MM-DD` or not a real calendar date) is rejected with the same `InvalidDateOfBirthError`.
+- The date of birth is validated before the e-mail lookup, so an invalid request stores nothing.
+- No minimum age or plausibility bound (for example before 1900): not requested.
+- Purpose "Identify the person": the request gives no other use. A later use (for example birthday journeys) changes the purpose in its own story.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Changing the date of birth after registration.
+- Adding the date of birth to the `identity.person-registered` event.
+- Birthday journeys (journey module).
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Purpose of `date_of_birth`: the request names none, so the column uses "Identify the person". The requester confirms it or gives the real use (for example an age check), before approval.
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
